    "rationale": "README states tmux-ide shows and connects agents but does not orchestrate them; Claude agent teams are Claude's own feature that it only displays.",
    "researcher": "researcher-batch08",
    "contentHash": "ac48265f4c5bd1a2070450d99ccfa0d233755f0c45adfa47ecc214c9b66afcc3",
    "review": {
      "state": "changes-requested",
      "reviewer": "agent:ADE-91",
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "contentHash": "ac48265f4c5bd1a2070450d99ccfa0d233755f0c45adfa47ecc214c9b66afcc3",
      "note": "COORD-03 was corrected: the product ships a skill (skill/SKILL.md, installed by integration install claude) that instructs an agent to task other running panes with send, read the fleet with team --json and wait on results, plus MCP and SDK tools. The README says tmux-ide does not orchestrate agents, and no lead role is designated. The first-party sources conflict on the coordinator facet, so 'no' is not established. Reinterpret under the coordinator rule (skill-instructed delegation to running sessions without a designated role) as yes, no or unknown."
    }
  },
